-- Cases for s 2(1), s 20(1) and s 47, taken from the text of the Act.  Expected values written by hand.
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Needs the time built-ins.
-- Each case that touches the First Schedule pins BOTH axes: the reading day (system time) and the conduct day
-- (valid time).  Two days are used throughout:
--   Date 1 6 2011 read on Date 1 8 2012   -> the three-item Schedule governs
--   Date 1 6 2011 read on Date 1 11 2012  -> the TVRO-only Schedule governs

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`
IMPORT `sgbau-sched-s549`
IMPORT `sgbau-first-schedule`
IMPORT `sgbau-act`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `Apparatus, transmissions and conduct, described by facts`

-- Television set, used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service.
`a television set` MEANS Apparatus WITH
    `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS TRUE
    `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS FALSE
    `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS TRUE
    `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS FALSE

-- The same facts, but the apparatus is NOT capable of (or designed or built for) reception: the control for the
-- first limb of s 2(1).
`a television-shaped box that cannot receive` MEANS Apparatus WITH
    `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS FALSE
    `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS FALSE
    `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS TRUE
    `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS FALSE

`a satellite dish system` MEANS Apparatus WITH
    `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS TRUE
    `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS FALSE
    `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS FALSE
    `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS TRUE

-- Programmes with pictures and sound, sent out for anyone with the equipment.
`an ordinary television service` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS TRUE
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS TRUE
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS TRUE
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS TRUE

`sound only, for anyone` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS FALSE
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS TRUE
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS FALSE
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS TRUE

-- Only the combination limb (c) of the definition is met.
`a combined programme only` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS FALSE
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS FALSE
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS TRUE
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS TRUE

-- Pictures, but not for persons having equipment appropriate: a private link, not a broadcasting service.
`a private picture link` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS TRUE
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS FALSE
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS FALSE
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS FALSE

`nothing received` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS FALSE
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS FALSE
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS FALSE
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS FALSE

GIVEN `what is received` IS A Transmission
      licensed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Conduct
`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`   IS FALSE
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`     IS FALSE
    `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`           IS TRUE
    `what is received on or by it`                                                              IS `what is received`
    `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`                      IS licensed

`an installer` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`   IS TRUE
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`     IS FALSE
    `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`           IS FALSE
    `what is received on or by it`                                                              IS `nothing received`
    `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`                      IS FALSE

`a dealer` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`   IS FALSE
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`     IS TRUE
    `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`           IS FALSE
    `what is received on or by it`                                                              IS `nothing received`
    `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`                      IS FALSE

§ `The question, with both axes pinned`

-- Both pins in one place for this module's cases: system time is the reading day, valid time the conduct day.
GIVEN question IS A BOOLEAN
      conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`as read on` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` reading (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` conduct question)

§ `Section 2(1): "broadcasting service"`

#ASSERT `it is a broadcasting service` `an ordinary television service` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a broadcasting service` `sound only, for anyone` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a broadcasting service` `a combined programme only` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a broadcasting service` `a private picture link` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `it is a broadcasting service` `nothing received` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 2(1): "broadcasting apparatus", under each text of the First Schedule`

-- Three-item text (conduct 1 June 2011, read 1 August 2012): a television set is broadcasting apparatus.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television set`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- TVRO-only text (read 1 November 2012): the same television set is not.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television set`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- The dish is broadcasting apparatus under both.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a satellite dish system`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a satellite dish system`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- The first limb: capable of, or designed or built for, reception.  The box that cannot receive is never
-- broadcasting apparatus, though its Schedule facts fit item 1.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television-shaped box that cannot receive`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television-shaped box that cannot receive`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- Outside the sources the answer is a refusal even where the first limb fails: the Schedule limb is asked first.
#ASSERT REFUSED `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television-shaped box that cannot receive`) (Date 1 1 2003) (Date 3 11 2026)
#ASSERT REFUSED `as read on` (`it is broadcasting apparatus` `a television set`) (Date 1 1 2003) (Date 3 11 2026)

§ `Section 20(1): the three limbs`

-- (c): operates, or has at home, broadcasting apparatus on or by which broadcasting services are received.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- (c) fails when nothing that is a broadcasting service is received on it.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `a private picture link` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `nothing received` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- (c) fails for the television once S 549/2012 is the text that governs, and holds for the dish.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a satellite dish system` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- (a): installs.  The installer receives nothing, so (c) is not the limb.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(a) applies` `a television set` `an installer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(a) applies` `a television set` `an installer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(a) applies` `a satellite dish system` `an installer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(c) applies` `a television set` `an installer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- (b): imports, offers for sale, sells, or has in possession with a view to sale.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(b) applies` `a television set` `a dealer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(b) applies` `a television set` `a dealer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1)(b) applies` `a satellite dish system` `a dealer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- s 20(1) as a whole.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) requires a licence` `a television set` `an installer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) requires a licence` `a television set` `a dealer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) requires a licence` `a television set` `a dealer`) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- "except under and in accordance with a licence": a licence means no contravention, though one was needed.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) is contravened` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) is contravened` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` TRUE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 20(1) requires a licence` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` TRUE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 47: the offence and what follows`

-- Offence under the three-item text: fine up to $40,000, imprisonment up to 3 years, forfeiture.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 47 offence is committed` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) (`s 47 greatest fine in dollars` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE))) EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) (`s 47 longest imprisonment in years` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE))) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 47 the apparatus would be forfeited on conviction` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- The same conduct read after the Notification: no offence, so no fine, no imprisonment, no forfeiture.
#ASSERT `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 11 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) (`s 47 greatest fine in dollars` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 11 2012) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) (`s 47 longest imprisonment in years` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 47 the apparatus would be forfeited on conviction` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- A licensed person commits no offence.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 47 offence is committed` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` TRUE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS FALSE
-- The dish owner: an offence under both texts.
#ASSERT `as read on` (`s 47 offence is committed` `a satellite dish system` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS TRUE
-- Outside the sources.
#ASSERT REFUSED `as read on` (`s 47 offence is committed` `a television set` (`a person who operates it at home, no licence needed unless licensed` `an ordinary television service` FALSE)) (Date 1 1 2003) (Date 3 11 2026)

§ `Two witnesses for the Notification's commencement agree`

-- sgbau-sched-s549.l4 says 1 January 2011 (from the Notification); BA1994.txt's Legislative History says the same.
#ASSERT `the Legislative History gives S 549/2012 a commencement of` EQUALS `S 549/2012 is deemed to have come into operation on`
